              "text": "yātrī is the nominative of yātrin \"being on a march or in a procession\", built from yātrā \"journey, pilgrimage\" with the suffix -in \"having\" (MW). \"A passenger\" is its modern use. yātrā comes from the root √yā \"go\"."
